% ============================================================================
% references.bib
%
% Source of truth for every work cited in the Article.
%
% NOTE ON USE. main.tex does NOT load a bibliography, and for a student-edited
% law review it should not: Bluebook wants full cites in footnotes with "supra
% note N" short forms, which is what the sections do. This file exists for two
% reasons. First, as a single checkable list of what is cited, so a claim can be
% traced without reading 155 footnotes. Second, because Berman raised the
% submission-venue question directly ("where do you plan on submitting this --
% to student-edited law reviews or to a peer-review journal? That would affect
% how this should be formatted"), and a peer-review submission would want
% author-date citations driven from here.
%
% To wire it up for a peer-review venue, add to the preamble:
%     \usepackage[authordate,backend=biber]{biblatex-chicago}
%     \addbibresource{references.bib}
% and \printbibliography at the end. Do NOT do this for a law review.
%
% Every entry below was transcribed from the manuscript's own footnotes, which
% were verified against primary sources in earlier passes. The `note` field
% records verification status. Anything not independently confirmed says so.
% ============================================================================


